# Who gets asked to review what.
#
# GitHub requests these reviewers automatically on any pull request touching a
# matching path. On its own that is a signal, not a gate: it becomes a gate when
# branch protection on the default branch has "Require review from Code Owners"
# turned on, which is available on public repositories.
#
# The point is not to keep people out. `bots/` is deliberately absent from this
# file: a submission is one folder, it is yours, and it needs no owner's opinion.
# What is listed here is the code that makes every recorded score mean something.

# The shared library. browser.py, game.py and runner.py are hashed into every
# recorded result because they drive the game, and init.js decides whether a seed
# replays at all.
/src/                       @pierpierpy

# The frozen harnesses. Each carries bot.py, render.py, bridge.js and init.js, and
# none of them is ever edited once a result exists beside it. A new idea is a new
# directory. See CONTRIBUTING.md.
/llm-bench/                 @pierpierpy

# The rules themselves, and the thing that enforces them.
/CONTRIBUTING.md            @pierpierpy
/.github/                   @pierpierpy
